On January 9th North and South Korea  engaged in high-level talks for the  first time in two years instead of  addressing North Korea's nuclear program  the two sides discussed less contentious  issues such as North Korea's  participation in the upcoming Winter  Olympics in Pyeongchang while dialogue  can reduce unnecessary tension and even  serve as a way to gather more  information about North Korea's  perspectives and strategy there could be  drawbacks of Washington and Seoul are  not careful first North Korea's  willingness to talk about minor issues  is not an indicator that Pyongyang's  position on nuclear weapons is softening  there is no situation under which North  Korea gives up its nuclear weapons  through negotiation second Kim might be  trying to improve relations with Seoul  as a way of driving a wedge in the  us-rok Alliance and there's a risk of  this given that the United States  prefers a strategy of escalating  pressure whereas South Korea prioritizes  maximum engagement now more than ever  the United States and South Korea must  continue to coordinate their approach  towards North Korea what do you think  about the potential thawing of relations  between North and South Korea let us  know in your comments also let us know  what other topics you'd like our  scholars to cover in 60 seconds and be  sure to LIKE and subscribe for more  research and videos from AEI
 

